            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous subclavian artery dissection: a pain in the neck diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2013-201223</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2013201223</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated subclavian artery dissection is a very rare condition in the absence of trauma or procedures. A 36-year-old woman with a history significant for uncontrolled hypertension presented with a sudden onset of left shoulder and neck pain that woke the patient from sleep. A CT angiogram of the chest revealed a left subclavian artery dissection. The patient was admitted to the hospital for blood pressure control.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
